To master Python systematically, practicing across structured difficulty tiers and domain-specific challenges is far more effective than tackling an unorganized list.

Here is a 1,000-problem curriculum broken down into four core phases, followed by the best platforms and repositories to source exact exercises.

1,000-Problem Roadmap
Phase	Level	Focus Areas	Problem Count
Phase 1	Beginner	Syntax, control flow, loops, basic math, string manipulation, and list basics	250 Problems
Phase 2	Intermediate	Dictionaries, sets, file I/O, regex, OOP principles, lambdas, and exception handling	250 Problems
Phase 3	Data Structures & Algorithms	Arrays, two-pointers, stacks/queues, recursion, linked lists, trees, graphs, and dynamic programming	300 Problems
Phase 4	Advanced & Applied	Concurrency/multiprocessing, decorators/generators, NumPy/Pandas data wrangling, API building, and mini-systems	200 Problems
Core Problem Breakdown by Phase
Phase 1: Beginner Fundamentals (250 Problems)
Variables & Arithmetic (50): Fahrenheit/Celsius conversions, compound interest calculators, leap year checkers, quadratic equation solvers, digit summation.

Control Flow & Logic (50): Prime number validators, FizzBuzz variants, largest of three numbers, grading systems, triangle type determination.

Loops & Patterns (50): Number pyramids, star patterns, factorial calculations, Fibonacci sequence generators, multiplication tables.

String Manipulation (50): Palindrome checks, anagram detection, vowel/consonant counters, Caesar cipher encrypter, title case converters.

Basic Lists & Tuples (50): Finding min/max/second largest, list reversal, duplicate removal, list rotations, cumulative sums.

Phase 2: Intermediate Python & OOP (250 Problems)
Dictionaries & Sets (60): Word frequency counters, dictionary merging, finding common keys/values, set operations (union/intersection), grouping anagrams.

Functions & Functional Tools (50): Recursion basics, map(), filter(), reduce(), arbitrary arguments (*args, **kwargs), lambda sorting.

Object-Oriented Programming (50): Bank account management system, library catalog, vehicle inheritance hierarchies, custom __repr__ and __str__ implementations, property getters/setters.

File Handling & Parsing (40): Reading/writing CSV and JSON files, log file parser, text file search-and-replace, batch file renamer.

Exceptions, Regex & Modules (50): Custom exception classes, email/URL validation regex, parsing phone numbers, date-time arithmetic with datetime.

Phase 3: Data Structures & Algorithms (300 Problems)
Arrays & Two Pointers (50): Two Sum, 3Sum, Container With Most Water, Trapping Rain Water, Subarray Sum Equals K.

Strings & Sliding Window (40): Longest substring without repeating characters, minimum window substring, string permutations.

Stacks & Queues (40): Valid parentheses, evaluate reverse Polish notation, min stack, sliding window maximum, monotonic stack problems.

Linked Lists (30): Reverse linked list, detect cycle, merge two sorted lists, LRU Cache implementation.

Trees & Graphs (70): Binary tree traversals (inorder/preorder/postorder), maximum depth, lowest common ancestor, BFS/DFS grid traversals, Dijkstra’s shortest path.

Dynamic Programming & Recursion (70): Climbing stairs, coin change, longest common subsequence, 0/1 knapsack, edit distance.

Phase 4: Advanced & Applied Python (200 Problems)
Python Internals & Metaprogramming (40): Custom decorators (timing, memoization, rate-limiting), custom generators/iterators, context managers (with statement), metaclasses.

Concurrency & Async (30): Web scrapers using asyncio and aiohttp, multi-threaded downloaders, producer-consumer queues using threading.

Data Science Essentials (NumPy/Pandas) (50): Matrix transformations, handling missing data, groupby aggregations, rolling window analytics, vectorization challenges.

System Design & Applied Projects (80):

Building a CLI-based task/expense tracker.

In-memory key-value store with TTL.

REST API using FastAPI with JWT authentication.

Custom mini web-framework/routing engine from scratch.

Where to Practice These Problems
Beginner & Intermediate: Exercism (Python Track) — 140+ mentored exercises focusing on idiomatic Python and clean code; Edabit — great for rapid-fire 10-minute challenges.

Data Structures & Algorithms: LeetCode (Blind 75 & NeetCode 150/300) — curated problem roadmaps covering standard DSA patterns; HackerRank (Python Domain) — for standard input/output and built-in library practice.

Applied & Project-Based: Project Euler — math-heavy logic puzzles; Advent of Code — 500+ real-world problem-solving challenges from past years.

